n_006 needs 2 H2O, and the pathway should make the quench into a cooler CO2-rich aqueous environment explicit rather than relying on the vague Biochemical label.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_006\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Rewrite rxn_006 as mol_008 + 2 mol_006 -> mol_012 + mol_003 + mol_007.\",\n        \"Specify the transition from hydrothermal synthesis to cooler CO2-rich aqueous trapping and hydrolysis conditions.\",\n        \"Consider adding the carbamate or ring-closure intermediate if mechanistic detail is desired.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.05\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.05,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.1,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.18,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.05,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.09,\n      \"feedback\": \"The literature does support glycine release from HCN oligomer hydrolysis, but not as the one-step reaction encoded here. rxn_008 is a ground-truth conservation violation: one HCN plus one water cannot produce two-carbon glycine, and the balance check indicates no simple small-species fix. This branch must be replaced by a multistep, mass-balanced oligomerization and hydrolysis subnetwork.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_008\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Replace rxn_008 with a multistep HCN oligomerization and hydrolysis module using multiple HCN equivalents and explicit intermediates such as DAMN or hydantoins.\",\n        \"Add the concentration regime and hydrolysis conditions that make the literature route plausible, such as eutectic or evaporative concentration and subsequent acid or base hydrolysis.\",\n        \"Do not keep this branch as a one-step shortcut because it violates elemental conservation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"re