y whether rxn_003 represents direct ammonolysis or staged cyanosulfidic chemistry.\",\n        \"If cyanosulfidic chemistry is intended, add the activating conditions or agents that make glycolonitrile-to-aminoacetonitrile plausible.\",\n        \"Write rxn_005 with 2 H2O and explicit aqueous hydrolysis conditions.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.91,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.74,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.87\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.82,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.85,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.6,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.95,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"feedback\": \"This route is coherent once aminoacetonitrile is available, and the glycinamide intermediate improves mechanistic clarity. The limiting issue remains rxn_003: the network should say whether this is staged photoredox or sulfide-assisted chemistry, or another activated surface process, not just generic 'surface conditions'.\",\n      \"approved\": true,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_003\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Clarify the activation and conditions for rxn_003.\",\n        \"Add explicit aqueous hydrolysis conditions for rxn_006 and rxn_007.\",\n        \"State whether the surface step and hydrolysis steps occur in the same microenvironment or after transfer.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.91,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.74,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.77,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.79\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.75,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.8,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.55,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.92,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.74,\n      \"feedback\": \"This is the weakest cyanide-surface route because it combines the under-specified glycolonitrile-to-aminoacetonitrile step with